{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Genetics and Neurodevelopment\n\nDomain hub: genetic architecture and measurement, and the developmental programme that builds the nervous system.\n\n[[Genetics and Neurodevelopment Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-27; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1730,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[DNA RNA and gene expression]]**\n*structure* - 6 sources\n\nThe molecules of inheritance and how information flows from DNA to protein, including the machinery that makes the flow regulated rather than mechanical.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Inheritance and variation]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nMendelian patterns, de novo variation, and how family and twin designs estimate genetic contribution.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 622,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Common and rare variants]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nTwo regimes of genetic architecture and why the distinction changes study design and interpretation.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 860,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genome-wide association studies]]**\n*method* - 3 sources\n\nHow GWAS works, what an association peak means, and the inference steps between a signal and a mechanism.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1098,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Polygenic scores and prediction]]**\n*method* - 8 sources\n\nWhat a polygenic score estimates, how it is validated, and the boundary between group-level research use and individual prediction.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1336,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Gene-environment interplay and epigenetics]]**\n*framework* - 9 sources\n\nInteraction, correlation and epigenetic marks: how environmental and genetic influences combine, and what the evidence does and does not show.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genes, environment and polygenic risk]]**\n*framework* - 13 sources\n\nCommon variants, genome-wide association, polygenic scores, fine-mapping and gene-environment interplay as the actual methods behind inheritance claims.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1884,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genetic inference and polygenic scores]]**\n*method* - 6 sources\n\nHow polygenic scores are built and validated, why transfer across populations is limited, and what individual-level inference they cannot support.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 2146,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Heritability and twin studies]]**\n*method* - 8 sources\n\nWhat heritability means and does not mean, how twin and family designs estimate it, the estimates for bipolar disorder, ADHD, autism and PTSD, and why measured variants explain less than twin studies suggest.",
			"x": 420,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Genetics",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 810,
			"height": 2102
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurogenesis and migration]]**\n*process* - 4 sources\n\nHow neurons are generated and reach their destinations, and why the framework for adult neurogenesis is more limited than popular accounts suggest.",
			"x": 880,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Axon guidance and synaptogenesis]]**\n*process* - 4 sources\n\nHow growing axons find targets using attractive and repulsive cues, and how initial synapses are formed and refined.",
			"x": 880,
			"y": 622,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Synaptic pruning and myelination]]**\n*process* - 6 sources\n\nExperience-dependent elimination of synapses and the progressive myelination of tracts, and why both change functional connectivity.",
			"x": 880,
			"y": 860,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Sensitive periods]]**\n*process* - 3 sources\n\nWindows of heightened experience-dependent plasticity, the circuit mechanisms that open and close them, and the limits of the evidence.",
			"x": 880,
			"y": 1122,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Development",
			"x": 850,
